    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0596" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11599.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Canada to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-22T06:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 22, 1914, 6 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Firing commenced again at daybreak. Ships now shelling southern part of city.
                    Large force men landed from Admiral Badger’s fleet before daylight. Copies of
                    proclamation issued by Admiral Fletcher requesting cooperation at once of
                    Alcalde, Jefe Político and <pb facs="0597" n="481" xml:id="pg481"/> populace of
                    Vera Cruz establishing order. Have sent messengers to locate these officials and
                    every effort is being made to that end. Unable yet communicate with Embassy but
                    expect to this morning as telegraph is working. Major Butler arrived with his
                    command during night from Tampico and is now ashore. Expected city will be
                    quieted this morning. No further information yet as to exact number killed and
                    wounded. Battleships <hi rendition="#italic">Florida, Utah, Arkansas, Vermont,
                        New Hampshire, New Jersey, South Carolina</hi>, transport <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Prairie</hi>, collier <hi rendition="#italic">Orion</hi>
                    now off this port. Transport <hi rendition="#italic">Hancock</hi> reported
                    due.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
